From 9555f5901a5d3e738b836f2d1dde6675bf92d096 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: "Max (macubuntu)" <mr.maksboi@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 28 Jul 2026 19:44:35 -0400
Subject: [PATCH] feat: add file_upload tool

Adds a file_upload tool covering the gap left by issues #247 and #88:
the server could download attachments but never upload anything.

Content comes from exactly one of three sources: file_path for a file on
disk, content for UTF-8 text, content_base64 for binary data such as a
screenshot taken in memory. Files are shared into a channel or thread via
files.getUploadURLExternal -> upload -> files.completeUploadExternal
(slack-go UploadFileContext), with initial_comment as the caption.

Verified working with browser session tokens (xoxc/xoxd), not just OAuth
and bot tokens. Earlier attempts assumed files.* rejects session tokens;
a full round trip against a live workspace shows it does not.

Security, addressing the reasons #121 and #285 were closed:
- tool is unregistered unless SLACK_MCP_FILE_UPLOAD_TOOL is set, and that
  variable doubles as a channel allowlist, same semantics as
  SLACK_MCP_ADD_MESSAGE_TOOL
- file_path is rejected entirely unless SLACK_MCP_FILE_UPLOAD_PATHS lists
  the directories the server may read; paths are resolved through symlinks
  and matched with filepath.Rel so a sibling sharing a name prefix cannot
  slip through
- the file is opened during validation with O_NOFOLLOW|O_NONBLOCK and every
  later step works off that descriptor, closing the TOCTOU window between
  the allowlist check and the read, and refusing FIFOs and devices
- channel is resolved before the allowlist check, so #general cannot be
  used to reach a channel the policy excludes
- request params are not logged, they carry the file payload

Uploads stream from the descriptor, so a 100MB cap does not mean 100MB of
memory. Windows keeps building: the open flags live in build-tagged files.

Co-Authored-By: Claude <noreply@anthropic.com>
